\[
    0
    \leq
    r_t(a) - r^H_t(a)
    \leq
    \ind{H < \tau_t(a) < \infty}.
\]
Taking conditional expectations given the realized history \(P_1,\dots,P_t\),
we get
\[
    \mathbb{E}\left[
        r_t(a) - r^H_t(a)
        \mid P_1,\dots,P_t
    \right]
    \leq
    \Pr\bigl[H < \tau_t(a) < \infty \mid P_1,\dots,P_t\bigr]
